  "slug": "dynamics-long-4a04",
  "summary": "Six preprints tie long-time and nonequilibrium dynamics to hidden correlations, symmetry asymmetry and quantum resources across circuits, mixed states and Hamiltonians.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is using dynamics and entanglement-type diagnostics to expose structure that local or static probes miss. One preprint proposes extracting a non-Hermitian topological invariant of Lindbladian spectra from covariance-matrix relaxation in open Gaussian systems. Others study entanglement and information dynamics in charged dual-unitary circuits with an impurity, which show non-monotonic entropy growth, and asymmetry dynamics of crosscap states, where local symmetry breaking grows while entanglement decreases. A decoherence-driven transition from a 1D SPT state to a product state reveals hidden long-range correlations. Two further works quantify genuine multipartite entanglement in Hubbard rings and relate quantum resources (entanglement, nonstabilizerness) to the onset of the QMC sign problem. These are heterogeneous in system and method, but all link nonlocal quantum structure to measurable dynamical or computational behavior.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
